<title>HUNGARY: Hungary to auction 3yr bonds of HUF40bln on Apr 10.</title>
<headline>Hungary to auction 3yr bonds of HUF40bln on Apr 10.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary will auction 40 billion forint worth of the three-year government bonds of 2000/E series on April 10, the Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said on Monday.</p>
<p>    First day of interest    18 April 1997</p>
<p>    Date of maturity	   12 May 2000</p>
<p>    Bonds on offer	 40,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Maximum yield		17.38 pct</p>
<p>    Minimum net price	  98.33 pct</p>
<p>Average yield at last</p>
<p>	 auction (March 13)</p>
<p>	 2000/D bond	     16.73 pct</p>
<p>Average price at last</p>
<p>	 auction		  105.32 pct</p>
<p>NOTE: The bond bears a fixed interest rate of 16.00 percent, payable semi-anually starting from April 18, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
